 156:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     *
 157:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * Enables the IMO to WCO lock feature. This function works only if the WCO is
 158:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * already enabled. If the WCO is not enabled then this function returns
 159:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * without enabling the lock feature.
 160:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     *
 161:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * It takes up to 20 ms for the IMO to stabilize. The delay is implemented with
 162:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * CyDelay() function. The delay interval is measured based on the system
 163:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * frequency defined by PSoC Creator at build time. If System clock frequency
 164:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * is changed in runtime, the CyDelayFreq() with the appropriate parameter
 165:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * should be called.
 166:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     *
 167:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * For PSoC 4200L devices, note that the IMO can lock to either WCO or USB
 168:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * but not both.
 169:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     *
 170:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * This function is applicable for PSoC 4100M / PSoC 4200M / PSoC 4000S /
 171:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLib.c ****     * PSoC 4100S / PSoC 4500 / PSoC Analog Coprocessor / PSoC 4200L.
